-07T11:00:00-08:00","expires":"2026-08-08T13:00:00-08:00","ends":"2026-08-08T13:00:00-08:00","status":"Actual","messageType":"Update","category":"Met","severity":"Severe","certainty":"Likely","urgency":"Expected","event":"Flood Warning","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","senderName":"NWS Anchorage AK","headline":"Flood Warning issued August 7 at 11:00AM AKDT until August 8 at 1:00PM AKDT by NWS Anchorage AK","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall continues.\n\n* WHERE...Yentna River including Lake Creek.\n\n* WHEN...Until 100 PM AKDT Saturday.\n\n* IMPACTS...Flooding of rivers, creeks, streams, and other low-lying\nand flood-prone locations is occurring.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 1053 AM AKDT, the river remains in moderate flood stage\nafter heavy rains earlier this week, but is beginning to\nsubside. The river crested at 22.52 ft around 8pm Thursday,\nAugust 7th.\n- For Yentna River at Lake Creek:\nAt 9:50am the stage was 22.3 feet.\nFlood Stage is 20.5 feet.\n\nImpacts:\nAt 20.5 feet: Anglers Inn & King Point Lodges will have water\nin several cabins.\n\n\n\nAt 22.0 feet: McDougal's, King Point, Anglers Inn, Wilderness\nPlace, Lake Creek Lodge, 3-Rivers, and Cottonwood Resorts\nwill have water in a number of cabins with water also\nencroaching the main lodge buildings.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood","instruction":"Stay tuned to further developments by listening to your local radio,\ntelevision, or NOAA Weather Radio for further information.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["FLWAFC"],"WMOidentifier":["WGAK48 PAFC 071900"],"NWSheadline":["FLOOD WARNING NOW IN EFFECT UNTIL 1 PM AKDT SATURDAY"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.EXT.PAFC.FA.W.0005.000000T0000Z-260808T2100Z/"],"eventEndingTime":["2026-08-08T13:00:00-08:00"]},"scope":"Public","code":"IPAWSv1.0","language":"en-US","web":"http://www.weather.gov","eventCode":{"SAME":["FLW"],"NationalWeatherService":["FAW"]}}},{"id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.413cea1636854e7ab77ba56d8a4a6c43a2284e73.001.1","type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-93.82,34],[-94.04,33.93],[-94.06,34.02],[-93.82,34.09],[-93.82,34]]]},"properties":{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.413cea1636854e7ab77ba56d8a4a6c43a2284e73.001.1","@type":"wx:Alert","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.413cea1636854e7ab77ba56d8a4a6c43a2284e73.001.1","areaDesc":"Howard, AR","geocode":{"SAME":["005061"],"UGC":["ARC061"]},"affectedZones":["https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/ARC061"],"references":[],"sent":"2026-08-08T10:58:00-05:00","effective":"2026-08-08T10:58:00-05:00","onset":"2026-08-08T10:58:00-05:00","expires":"2026-08-08T13:00:00-05:00","ends":"2026-08-08T13:00:00-05:00","status":"Actual","messageType":"Alert","category":"Met","severity":"Severe","certainty":"Likely","urgency":"Immediate","event":"Flash Flood Warning","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","senderName":"NWS Shreveport LA","headline":"Flash Flood Warning issued August 8 at 10:58AM CDT until August 8 at 1:00PM CDT by NWS Shreveport LA","description":"FFWSHV\n\nThe National Weather Service in Shreveport has issued a\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nEast Central Howard County in southwestern Arkansas...\n\n* Until 100 PM CDT.\n\n* At 1058 AM CDT, Doppler radar indicated thunderstorms producing\nheavy rain across the warned area. Between 1 and 3 inches of rain\nhave fallen. The expected rainfall rate is 1 to 2 inches in 1 hour.\nAdditional rainfall amounts of 1 to 2 inches are possible in the\nwarned area. Flash flooding is ongoing or expected to begin\nshortly.\n\nHAZARD...Flash flooding caused by thunderstorms.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Flash flooding of small creeks and streams, urban areas,\nhighways, streets and underpasses as well as other poor\ndrainage and low-lying areas.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nCorinth and Center Point.","instruction":"Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nBe aware of your surroundings and do not drive on flooded roads.\n\nPlease report observed flooding to local emergency services or law\nenforcement and request they pass this information to the National\nWeather Service when you can do so safely.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["FFWSHV"],"WMOidentifier":["WGUS54 KSHV 081558"],"flashFloodDetection":["RADAR INDICATED"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.NEW.KSHV.FF.W.0070.260808T1558Z-260808T1800Z/"],"eventEndingTime":["2026-08-08T13:00:00-05:00"]},"scope":"Public","code":"IPAWSv1.0","language":"en-US","web":"http://www.weather.gov","eventCode":{"SAME":["FFW"],"NationalWeatherService":["FFW"]}}},{"id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e2aaa71baead7a686ec835c0c3d535257a7be5b0.001.1","type":"Feature","geometry":{"type":"Polygon","coordinates":[[[-93.75,34.01],[-93.82,34.01],[-93.82,34.09],[-93.68,34.13],[-93.61,34.24],[-93.52,34.24],[-93.5,34.21],[-93.45,34.17],[-93.49,34.12],[-93.64,33.98],[-93.74,34],[-93.75,34.01]]]},"properties":{"@id":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e2aaa71baead7a686ec835c0c3d535257a7be5b0.001.1","@type":"wx:Alert","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e2aaa71baead7a686ec835c0c3d535257a7be5b0.001.1","areaDesc":"Pike, AR","geocode":{"SAME":["005109"],"UGC":["ARC109"]},"affectedZones":["https://api.weather.gov/zones/county/ARC109"],"references":[],"sent":"2026-08-08T09:55:00-05:00","effective":"2026-08-08T09:55:00-05:00","onset":"2026-08-08T09:55:00-05:00","expires":"2026-08-08T13:00:00-05:00","ends":"2026-08-08T13:00:00-05:00","status":"Actual","messageType":"Alert","category":"Met","severity":"Severe","certainty":"Likely","urgency":"Immediate","event":"Flash Flood Warning","sender":"w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov","senderName":"NWS Little Rock AR","headline":"Flash Flood Warning issued August 8 at 9:55AM CDT until August 8 at 1:00PM CDT by NWS Little Rock AR","description":"FFWLZK\n\nThe National Weather Service in Little Rock has issued a\n\n* Flash Flood Warning for...\nCentral Pike County in southwestern Arkansas...\n\n* Until 100 PM CDT.\n\n* At 955 AM CDT, Doppler radar indicated thunderstorms producing\nheavy rain across the warned area. Between 1 and 3 inches of rain\nhave fallen in the last hour. The expected rainfall rate is 2 to 4\ninches per hour. Flash flooding is ongoing or expected to begin\nshortly.\n\nHAZARD...Flash flooding caused by thunderstorms.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Flash flooding of small creeks and streams, urban areas,\nhighways, streets and underpasses as well as other poor\ndrainage and low-lying areas.\n\n* Some locations that will experience flash flooding include...\nMurfreesboro, Crater Of Diamonds State Park, Pike City, Roy and\nHighland in Pike County.","instruction":"Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.\n\nIn hilly terrain there are hundreds of low water crossings which are\npotentially dangerous in heavy rain. Do not attempt to cross flooded\nroads. Find an alternate route.\n\nFlooding is occurring or is imminent. It is important to know where\nyou are relative to streams, rivers, or creeks which can become\nkillers in heavy rains. Campers and hikers should avoid streams or\ncreeks.","response":"Avoid","note":null,"parameters":{"AWIPSidentifier":["FFWLZK"],"WMOidentifier":["WGUS54 KLZK 081455"],"flashFloodDetection":["RADAR INDICATED"],"BLOCKCHANNEL":["EAS","NWEM","CMAS"],"EAS-ORG":["WXR"],"VTEC":["/O.NEW.KLZK.FF.W.0066.260808T1455Z-260808T1800Z/"],"eventEndingTime":["2026-08-08T13:00:00-05:00"]},"scope":"Public","code":"IPAWSv1.0","language":"en-US","web":"http://www.weather.gov","eventCode":{"SAME":["FFW"],"NationalWeatherService":["FFW"]}}}]}